#====================================================================
# Draft: upstream test data fetched from an external GitHub repo whose
#        master path moved (404) — recover via git sparse clone of the
#        data repo + CSV format adaptation + regenerate per upstream
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-ASTRONOMY-2.1.9-UPSTREAM-TEST-DATA-EXTERNAL-REPO-DRIFT
trigger_tool:           astronomy|generate/run|make_constellation_data.py|git|curl|ctest
phase:                  test
error_signature:        Cannot open input file: constellation/test_input.txt|hygdata_v3.csv.*404|raw.githubusercontent.com/astronexus|HYG-Database

severity:               2
category:               test-data-drift
match_keywords:         upstream test data, external GitHub repo, raw.githubusercontent, /raw/, 404, repo restructure, git sparse clone, blob:none, CSV, quoted CSV, regenerate test data, constellation, HYG-Database, test input

title:                  Upstream test scripts that hardcode a raw.githubusercontent.com path into an external data repo break after the repo restructures; recover by git sparse-cloning the data repo, adapting the data format, and regenerating the test input with the upstream generator

root_cause:             astronomy's generate/run downloads hygdata_v3.csv from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astronexus/HYG-Database/master/hygdata_v3.csv, then make_constellation_data.py turns it into constellation/test_input.txt used by ctest. The external repo restructured (root file moved to hyg/v3/hyg_v3X.csv.gz), so every mirror of the hardcoded URL returns 404 and the ConstellationTest has no input file.

affected_scope:         Any package whose upstream test suite downloads fixed paths (raw.githubusercontent / /raw/ / master) from an external data repo that may be restructured; verified instance - astronomy 2.1.9 ConstellationTest.

verification_cmd:       python3 make_constellation_data.py && ./ctest all (ConstellationTest PASS with 117958 cases)

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           git-sparse-clone-same-generation-data-plus-format-adaptation
rec_description:        Do not patch the upstream test script. Recover the data from the same repository generation: git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse <repo> && git sparse-checkout set <subdir> to fetch only the needed data files over a working mirror (e.g. gh-proxy); pick the same-generation data version the upstream generator expects; if the repo now stores quoted CSV but the generator expects plain headers, convert with Python's csv module (reader->writer, no quoting); then run the upstream generator exactly as written. Verify by running the affected test and reporting the generated case count.
rec_command:            git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://gh-proxy.com/https://github.com/astronexus/HYG-Database hygclone && cd hygclone && git sparse-checkout set hyg/v3 && gunzip -k hyg/v3/hyg_v33.csv.gz && python3 -c "import csv; ...plain csv..." && cd .. && python3 make_constellation_data.py && ./ctest all
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               none (data recovery only; no source patch)

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      report-external-data-unavailable
fallback_description:   If the external repo is fully deleted or the exact byte-identical version is required and unavailable, keep the affected upstream test unrun, list it in the ledger with the query commands/exit codes/times, and give the recovery condition (archive restore or upstream re-publish).
fallback_command:       curl -fsSL -o hygdata_v3.csv <every mirror URL>; record each exit code
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       commit a hand-written fake constellation/test_input.txt into the archive|patch make_constellation_data.py to read a different column layout silently|pretend the test passed
forbid_1_reason:        Fabricated test inputs hide real engine coverage; silently changing the generator diverges from upstream; fake passes violate evidence rules.
forbid_1_consequence:   Quality-fail on review; test statistics invalidated.

principles:             real-evidence-over-assumption, upstream-fidelity, reproducible-test-input, minimal-patch
